      <title>Notes around SIDOsc (1)</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/blog/sidosc/</link>
      <pubDate>Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/blog/sidosc/</guid>
      <description>&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I spent quite a bit of my childhood in front of a Commodore 64, and one sound always stuck with me. It created this sensation of thinning out and thickening again while keeping the same pitch. Listen to the opening of Wally Beben&amp;rsquo;s &lt;code&gt;Dark Side&lt;/code&gt; (1988/89) for a classic example:&#xA;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;div style=&#34;max-width: 560px; margin: 1.5em auto;&#34;&gt;&#xA;&lt;div style=&#34;position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden;&#34;&gt;&#xA;      &lt;iframe allow=&#34;accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share; fullscreen&#34; loading=&#34;eager&#34; referrerpolicy=&#34;strict-origin-when-cross-origin&#34; src=&#34;https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/_JWxbhRify0?autoplay=0&amp;amp;controls=1&amp;amp;end=0&amp;amp;loop=0&amp;amp;mute=0&amp;amp;start=0&#34; style=&#34;position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border:0;&#34; title=&#34;YouTube video&#34;&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#xA;    &lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;/div&gt;&#xA;&lt;br&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;d hiss air through my teeth while sweeping my palm back and forth in front of my face to imitate it. Years later, while working on &lt;a href=&#34;https://github.com/hayakzan/SIDOsc&#34;&gt;SIDOsc&lt;/a&gt;, I finally got to catch some insight about how this worked.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
